16
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.807
to describe the indescribable.

17
00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:56.640
Thank you.

18
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.670
Well, I was just gonna say the book started

19
00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:02.418 line:15%
as prose that I wanted to write for my children basically.

20
00:01:02.418 --> 00:01:04.938 line:15%
And it was just sort of snippets of my life.

21
00:01:04.938 --> 00:01:06.200 line:15%
And you sort of get to a place in your life

22
00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.320 line:15%
where you're like, oh I want them always,

23
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.500 line:15%
I want them to remember.

24
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.730 line:15%
I want them to know about me

25
00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.810 line:15%
and their lives and where they came from.

26
00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.423 line:15%
So it kind of was born out of that.

27
00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:19.970
And lo and behold, it became a book,

28
00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.970
but it was intended as sort of just for my kids.

29
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.083
It reads very poetically too.

30
00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:31.960
There's, I know you're a rock and roll musician.

31
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.242
Music has been such an integral part of your life

32
00:01:35.242 --> 00:01:39.370
and it has sort of a beatnik, poetic, one word sentences

33
00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.560
and then you go down.

34
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.640 line:15%
And I grew up obsessed with poetry

35
00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.090 line:15%
and I just thought there are no rules to writing.

36
00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.140
You actually want your reader to read

37
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.670
the way it is in your mind.

38
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.833
And you just do such a beautiful job of it.

39
00:01:53.973 --> 00:01:55.680
Thank you so much.

40
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.477
It was really a labor of love

41
00:01:57.477 --> 00:01:59.363
and it was one of the hardest things I've ever done.

42
00:02:00.274 --> 00:02:01.452
What I love about your book,

43
00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:02.973
and this is the ultimate Mother's Day read,

44
00:02:04.073 --> 00:02:06.240
is that we come into this world

45
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.090
with our own history with our moms.

46
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.030
And then we're just as moms trying to do the best we can,

47
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.590
not repeat patterns, break cycles.

48
00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:20.210
And just the way that you spoke about your first daughter,

49
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:25.210
your oldest daughter was something I just hadn't read

50
00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:28.610
because I felt so connected to you.

51
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.180
I'm so scared of whatever I'm doing,

52
00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.330
especially with my first born daughter, Olive.

53
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.980
There's a different relationship there

54
00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:36.950
than there is with Frankie.

55
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.393
The love is equal, but the karma is different.

56
00:02:42.491 --> 00:02:46.123
And I just hadn't read anyone who kind of had the humor

57
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.070
without being best friend-y.

58
00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.050
It was like, you talked about the role reversals

59
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:55.000
you go through as you grow up together.

60
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.772
Yes, we definitely do and you, and I find that

61
00:02:59.772 --> 00:03:03.760
that role reversal has been as enlightening for me

62
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.760
as it is for her, as long as I kind of stay in step with it.

63
00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.130
You know, I think that, I've always been really honest

64
00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:13.963
with my children.

65
00:03:13.963 --> 00:03:17.306
I have told them things that,

66
00:03:17.306 --> 00:03:19.410
so that I've always wanted them to feel

67
00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.150
and I have wanted, and they do,

68
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.200
that there's an open door, that they can always talk

69
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.403
to me about everything.

70
00:03:25.553 --> 00:03:28.450
And because it's a big, wide scary world

71
00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.280
out there sometimes.

72
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.630
So you want to be, and this was something I couldn't do

73
00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.760
with my own parents.

74
00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.850
I went through a lot of stuff that I just didn't feel safe

75
00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.063
telling them about.

76
00:03:38.285 --> 00:03:40.690
And I never wanted to, and I don't, I still don't,

77
00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:45.690
I don't want to create that non place for them.

78
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:50.700
I want them to be able to have open conversation.

79
00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.090
My thing with them is always like, look,

80
00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.490
if you tell me the truth and it's something that

81
00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.100
we don't like, it's better that you told me the truth.

82
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.653
You'll get in less trouble if you tell me the truth.

83
00:04:03.653 --> 00:04:05.380
So that's kind of where I come from with it.

84
00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.910
I'm so relieved to hear you say that

85
00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.276
'cause I say the same things to my kids all the time.

86
00:04:10.276 --> 00:04:12.700
And even if it's something I don't like, I will give it time

87
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.530
and then circle back to what we need to fix about that.

88
00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:22.070
But in that moment, I'm like, let this secret be safe.

89
00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.500
Let me be a safe place that's not gonna respond immediately

90
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.710
or judge or punish or anything.

91
00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.910
I don't want to react, I just want to listen

92
00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.210
and then we'll get there.

93
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.961
Don't worry, we'll get there.

94
00:04:32.961 --> 00:04:34.729
Yeah, oh yeah, yeah, we get there.

95
00:04:34.729 --> 00:04:36.192
We're going to deal with this.

96
00:04:36.192 --> 00:04:38.637
And I'm so glad to hear you say that

97
00:04:38.637 --> 00:04:43.161
and really this is a book that needs to be read by mothers.

98
00:04:43.161 --> 00:04:45.720
It's, no matter what your experience with your own family

99
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.920
or what you're going through with your kids,

100
00:04:49.196 --> 00:04:52.530
there is honesty, humor, and triumph in your perspective

101
00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:55.740
that's very fresh and different than other books I've read.

102
00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.780
Wow, Drew, this is so nice to hear you say all this

103
00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.740
because I feel good about that book too.

104
00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.430
It's been out for a couple of years, so thank you.

105
00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.290
I really, really appreciate that.

106
00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.873 line:15%
(upbeat music)

